Experiment 1.1 Contain Duplicates (217)

Aim : Given an integer array nums, return true if any value appears at least twice in the array, and return false if every element is distinct.

Algorithm : 1. Create an empty set called seen.
            2. Traverse each element num in the array.
            3. Check if num is already present in seen.
               If Yes, return True because a duplicate is found.
            4. Otherwise, add num to seen.
            5. Continue until all elements are checked.
            6. If the loop finishes without finding any duplicate, return False

Code :

class Solution(object):
    def containsDuplicate(self, nums):
        
        nums.sort()  
        for i in range(1, len(nums)):
            if nums[i] == nums[i - 1]: 
                return True
        return False




Experiment 1.2 Contain Duplicates2 (219)

Aim : Given an integer array nums and an integer k, return true if there are two distinct indices i and j in the array such that nums[i] == nums[j] and abs(i - j) <= k.

Algorithm :
ContainsNearbyDuplicate(nums, k)
1. Create an empty dictionary last_index.
2. For each index i and element num in nums:
      a. If num exists in last_index:
            i. Calculate distance = i - last_index[num]
           ii. If distance ≤ k:
                   Return True
      b. Store the current index:
            last_index[num] = i
3. Return False


Code :

class Solution:
    def containsNearbyDuplicate(self, nums, k):
        last_index = {}
        for i, num in enumerate(nums):
            if num in last_index and i - last_index[num] <= k:
                return True
            last_index[num] = i
        return False
